SUMMARY:Third Friday - Art Gallery Reception in Downtown Durham
DESCRIPTION:Celebrate two NEW exhibitions at the DAC:\nDa Da Da: Trios by Jennifer Clifton\nThrough sculpture\, drawing\, and installation\, Jennifer Clifton explores repetition\, pattern\, and connection\, inviting viewers to consider the relationships formed through groupings of three.\nRewoven: What We Leave Behind by Jen Stone\nThis mixed-media textile exhibition examines memory\, loss\, and resilience through fiber-based works that reflect on the marks we leave behind and the stories that continue to shape us.\nAnd don’t miss your last chance to see Natural/Unnatural\, presented by the Durham Art Guild\, this exhibition features works by Emily Clare and Kelsey Merreck Wagner that explore the intersections and tensions between the natural and constructed worlds.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/third-friday-art-gallery-reception-in-downtown-durham/
LOCATION:Durham Arts Council\, 120 Morris Street\, DURHAM\, NC\, NC\, 27701\, United States
CATEGORIES:Art
